      "seq": 21,
      "kind": "submit",
      "at": 1791588766619,
      "reason": "apply_merges: when the lowest-rank pair occurs only once (the common case for short regex chunks), splice it in place (ids[j]=idx; del ids[j+1]; del ranks[j]) and recompute just the two neighbouring ranks instead of rebuilding the ids and ranks lists. ids is copied once up front so the caller's list is never mutated. Multi-occurrence merges keep the existing path. Output is identical (equivalence passed); encode_ir ratio 0.9115."
